WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.616
This ERD shows the logical blueprint for

00:00:02.629 --> 00:00:06.794
the clinic Patient and provider each connect

00:00:06.821 --> 00:00:10.415
to appointment Appointment then connects to service

00:00:10.442 --> 00:00:14.632
through the appointment service junction table Read

00:00:14.658 --> 00:00:17.106
each relationship separately rather than trying to

00:00:17.132 --> 00:00:21.597
understand the entire diagram at once Patient

00:00:21.623 --> 00:00:25.481
to appointment is one-to-many Provider to
appointment

00:00:25.494 --> 00:00:29.376
is one-to-many Appointment to service is
many-to-many

00:00:29.586 --> 00:00:33.812
so appointment service sits between them Notice

00:00:33.839 --> 00:00:36.154
that appointment service also stores facts about

00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:38.575
the relationship such as quantity and unit

00:00:38.602 --> 00:00:41.828
charge Those values do not belong only

00:00:41.854 --> 00:00:43.512
to the appointment or only to the

00:00:43.525 --> 00:00:46.894
service They belong to the specific service

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:50.735
used in a specific appointment That is

00:00:50.762 --> 00:00:52.972
one reason junction tables are often real

00:00:52.985 --> 00:00:55.854
business entities rather than only technical
connectors
